<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <CustomField> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find
        matching parent xml file" error.

        DISPOSITION GAP CLOSURE TRANCHE 1, ITEM 6 (agent-output/disposition-gap-closure-t1-design.md
        §3 Item 6, premises P-1/P-2/P-3, decisions D-3/D-4, both settled at Gate 1 2026-08-31).

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 THIS IS AN ADDITIVE NEW FIELD, NOT A CONVERSION OF Days_On_Market__c. SALESFORCE
        CANNOT CHANGE AN EXISTING CUSTOM FIELD INTO A FORMULA FIELD - THERE IS NO IN-PLACE TYPE
        CHANGE TO FORMULA VIA THE UI OR THE METADATA API (P-1). Converting in place would be a
        DELETE + CREATE, and a deleted API name stays RESERVED until manually ERASED in Setup
        (irreversible, and blocked while any Apex still references it). The additive route below
        is this repo's standing pattern (see Asking_Price__c and BOV_Score__c's own headers:
        "the field itself is NOT deleted (additive retirement, per this repo's standing rule)").

        Days_On_Market__c (the existing stored Number(4,0)) IS NOT TOUCHED, IS NOT DELETED, AND
        ITS editable=true GRANT IN DPEG_Disposition_Edit STAYS LEGAL - none of that would be true
        under an in-place conversion, where editable=true on a formula field is a hard Metadata
        API deploy error. Its own field header in BrokerListingSelector.cls:53-57 already states
        it is "LEGACY: a hand-keyed Number that nothing writes", retained on purpose.

        =====================================================================================
        API NAME: Days_On_Market_Live__c (decision D-4). Shorthand, flagged as such, not
        invented independently - Days_On_Market__c is occupied on this same object by the stored
        field, so the additive pattern forces a new name.
        =====================================================================================

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 THIS IS RAW ELAPSED DAYS. IT IS NOT, AND MUST NEVER BE TREATED AS, THE ESCALATION
        CLOCK (decision D-3, premise P-3).
        =====================================================================================
        DispositionStageEntryService:1008-1011 leaves this listing's Days_On_Market__c blank on
        purpose on auto-create - "seeding a 0 would resurrect the very field the clock was moved
        OFF." The marketing clock was deliberately moved OFF the listing entirely and into
        DispositionTractionService.evaluate, which computes days in Apex and, per the pending
        design at agent-output/listing-alerts-and-escalation.md §7.2, is to gain a PAUSE at first
        offer. This formula has NO pause and NO knowledge of offers - it is TODAY() minus
        List_Date__c, unconditionally, for as long as the listing has a list date. It WILL
        disagree with the badge DispositionTractionService renders beside it once an offer
        arrives and the traction clock pauses while this formula keeps counting. THAT IS
        EXPECTED AND ACCEPTED (D-3: ship the formula now) - not a bug to reconcile.
        NOTHING MAY READ THIS FORMULA TO DRIVE AN ALERT OR ESCALATION. Alert/escalation logic
        belongs to DispositionTractionService alone. This is now the THIRD days-on-market
        definition in this application, on purpose: Disposition__c.Days_On_Market__c (a separate,
        also-raw formula off Listing_Date__c on the Disposition), this field (raw, off
        Broker_Listing__c.List_Date__c), and DispositionTractionService's paused Apex clock. Do
        not merge them.

        =====================================================================================
        THE FORMULA - MIRRORS Disposition__c.Days_On_Market__c EXACTLY, PER INSTRUCTION.
        =====================================================================================
            IF(ISBLANK(List_Date__c), null, TODAY() - List_Date__c)
        Returns null, not 0, for a listing with no list date - the in-repo precedent for a Number
        formula answering "not yet datable" (see BOV_Score__c's header for the general form of
        the 0-vs-null trap this avoids). formulaTreatBlanksAs is BlankAsZero, matching the
        Disposition__c precedent's exact shape - the explicit ISBLANK guard makes the blanks
        setting moot in practice, mirrored rather than varied because this exact enum spelling on
        a fresh Number formula field cannot be confirmed without MCP (GATE G-4, per
        salesforce-global-rule.md; mcp=unavailable). A bad enum spelling fails loudly at deploy,
        which is the safe direction if the mirroring is somehow wrong.

        =====================================================================================
        CONSUMERS - NONE REPOINTED BY THIS FILE. LISTED SO THE DEVELOPER AGENT'S SCOPE IS CLEAR.
        =====================================================================================
        - BrokerListingSelector.selectMostRecentByDispositionId:71 - DEV TASK: repoint
          Days_On_Market__c -> Days_On_Market_Live__c. Widening that WITH USER_MODE field list is
          an FLS change; the read grant for THIS field must land in the SAME deploy as the
          selector change (consolidated permission-set pass owns the grant; this file does not).
        - lwc/brokerListing / BrokerListingController:132-139 - NO CHANGE. Computes days in Apex
          from the raw date; reads neither Number field.
        - DispositionStageEntryService:1008-1011 - NO SCHEMA CHANGE, but its own comment ("seeding
          a 0 would resurrect the very field the clock was moved OFF") is now stale wording since
          a formula cannot be seeded at all - DEV TASK to amend that comment in place.
        - DPEG_Disposition_Edit's editable=true grant on Days_On_Market__c - UNCHANGED, and
          correctly so: it names the STORED field, not this one.
        - 3 seed scripts (seed-disposition.apex:217, seed-disposition-bulk.apex:372/377/382/387,
          seed-disp0002.apex:183) assign Days_On_Market__c (the stored field) - UNCHANGED, not
          this field, no compile risk under the additive route.
        - objectTranslations/Broker_Listing__c-en_US/ gains a sibling translation file for this
          field in the same pass as this file (see that directory).

        =====================================================================================
        🔴 RETIRING Disposition__c.Days_On_Market__c IS NOT PART OF THIS CHANGE AND IS BLOCKED.
        =====================================================================================
        reports/Dispositions/Avg_Days_on_Market.report-meta.xml is reportType
        CustomEntity$Disposition__c and its only measure is Disposition__c.Days_On_Market__c. A
        report on the Disposition report type cannot show a Broker_Listing__c field - no
        Disposition-with-Broker-Listing report type exists in this repo, so repointing that report
        needs a NEW report type, out of scope here. Reports do not block field deletion; they
        break silently (memory: field-rename-traps) - so deleting the Disposition copy without
        repointing the report first would leave a dashboard component rendering nothing with no
        error anywhere. NEITHER Disposition__c.Days_On_Market__c NOR its
        Disposition_Dashboard_Access grant is touched by this change; retirement is a named,
        deferred follow-up (design doc §5 wave 8), not actioned here.

        FLS: read-only in both disposition sets (this is a computed field; editable=true on a
        formula is a deploy error regardless). Applied in the consolidated permission-set pass,
        not this file.

        Risk: HIGH per the design doc - the highest-risk item in the tranche, though the hazards
        (formula-conversion mechanics, editable=true trap, report/report-type blocker) all apply
        to the CONVERSION route this file deliberately does NOT take. As shipped (purely additive)
        the residual risk is the D-3 "third definition" disagreement, which is accepted by design.
    -->
    <fullName>Days_On_Market_Live__c</fullName>
    <externalId>false</externalId>
    <formula>IF(ISBLANK(List_Date__c), null, TODAY() - List_Date__c)</formula>
    <formulaTreatBlanksAs>BlankAsZero</formulaTreatBlanksAs>
    <description>RAW ELAPSED DAYS since List_Date__c. NOT the escalation clock - DispositionTractionService owns pause semantics for alerting; nothing may read this formula to drive an alert. See the XML comment in this file for the full reasoning (additive vs conversion, and why a third days-on-market definition exists on purpose).</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Days since this listing&apos;s List Date, computed live. This is a raw count, not the paused marketing/escalation clock shown elsewhere - it will keep counting after an offer arrives.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Days on Market (Live)</label>
    <precision>18</precision>
    <required>false</required>
    <scale>0</scale>
    <trackHistory>false</trackHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>Number</type>
    <unique>false</unique>
</CustomField>
